<title>JAPAN: Tokyo March consumer prices unchanged yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Tokyo March consumer prices unchanged yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tokyo area consumer prices stayed unchanged in March from a year earlier, while nationwide consumer prices for February increased 0.6 percent from a year earlier, the government's Management and Coordination Agency said on Friday.</p>
<p>In fiscal 1996/97, Tokyo consumer prices rose 0.1 percent from the previous year.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of consumer prices in Tokyo and nationwide (index base 1995):</p>
<p>					MAR	FEB	JAN</p>
<p> Tokyo overall index	    99.8     99.7     99.8</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr changes		 0.0pct  0.0pct   0.0pct</p>
<p>  mth-on-mth changes	    +0.1pct  -0.1pct  -0.1pct</p>
<p> Tokyo core index		 100.0    99.8     99.8</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr changes		+0.1pct  +0.1pct  +0.1pct</p>
<p>  mth-on-mth changes	    +0.2pct   0.0pct  -0.2pct</p>
<p>					FEB	JAN	DEC</p>
<p> Nationwide overall index     100.1    100.3    100.4</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr changes		 +0.6pct  +0.6pct  +0.6pct</p>
<p>  mth-on-mth changes	     -0.2pct  -0.1pct  +0.1pct</p>
<p> Nationwide core index	  100.0    100.1    100.5</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr changes		 +0.4pct  +0.5pct  +0.3pct</p>
<p>  mth-on-mth changes	     -0.1pct  -0.4pct  -0.1pct</p>
<p>(Note: The Tokyo index is calculated by collecting price data at mid-month. The core index, which is a key barometer for gauging core inflation, is overall prices minus fresh food prices. The base year has been changed to 1995 from 1990.)</p>
</text>
